# Part 5, rows 8 and 9: a `test` becomes a zero-argument function (entered only
# by `heroes test`), and `assert` becomes a branch plus an abort that carries
# the source text AND both sides — the spec promises both. The call is written
# `add(a: 2, b: 3)` because §4.9 makes labels mandatory when two parameters
# share a type: this case was written without them and the compiler refused it.
function add(a: int, b: int) -> int
    return a + b

test "addition holds"
    assert add(a: 2, b: 3) == 5
